---
// VISUAILS — /compare (English). The page body lives in ComparePage.astro so
// that /compare and /nl/compare cannot drift apart; only the meta differs here.
//
// AUDIT-TASK-0.md §F: "REWRITE, URL kept. Becomes 'Shoot day vs VISUAILS'."
// The AI-tools argument is not dropped from the site — it survives as the
// #ai-tools section inside ComparePage, which /custom-models links into, and
// the title still carries the "AI" search intent alongside the new one.
//
// The meta description is built from pricing.js: a price typed into a <meta>
// tag is the one place a stale figure survives a page rewrite. The old
// description was 207 characters — well past the ~160 Google renders.
//
// It also quoted a package against a day — "a drop is €1,850 for 25–30
// products" — and there is no package now (section 0 of src/data/pricing.js).
// A falling rate cannot be set against a day's cost without naming a count, so
// this quotes the same WORKED EXAMPLE the page body's right-hand column does,
// at the same count, from quote(). If ANCHOR_PRODUCTS moves in
// ComparePage.astro, it moves here.
//
// BOTH SIDES CARRY ONE VAT LABEL. Every figure in pricing.js is net, including
// the shoot-day range, so one label covers the pair — and a comparison that
// prints a net figure beside a gross one flatters us by a fifth without the
// reader being able to see it happen.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ComparePage from '../components/ComparePage.astro';
import { SHOOT_DAY, euro, quote, vatLabel } from '../data/pricing.js';

const ANCHOR_PRODUCTS = 30;

const description =
  `A production day runs ${SHOOT_DAY.en.range}. ${ANCHOR_PRODUCTS} products ` +
  `here is ${euro(quote('complete', ANCHOR_PRODUCTS).net, 'en')}, both ` +
  `${vatLabel('excl', 'en')}. Including where a shoot day still wins.`;
---

<Layout title="Shoot day vs VISUAILS — the honest comparison" description={description}>
  <ComparePage lang="en" />
</Layout>
